! The test architecture, planned before it moves

The operator (2026-11-19, verbatim): "Send 2 Fable scout for the test-architecture total-refactor planning … That's crud we need to clean up, but we need a design plan first so we don't sacrifice coverage for less-test-wall-clock-time." Earlier the same night: "Too much wall time burnt on testing.... ugh. Anything we can do to move this along and let CI handle testing?" (now lane law: spirits run their red/green tests and the tests beside touched files; CI's full run carries the verdict).

Both handbacks rest below whole. Neither seer could read `lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/research/test-estate-astra` (the house stood at its floor that night), so reconciling against it opens every test lane.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/decisions`>>

!! The five decisions (landed by Lares-Alpha on the operator's word: "Talk through the questions and land decisions yourselves"; each open to overturn)

# ''Affected-test selection on the lane doorstep'': yes, as an addition, never a replacement; develop and the merge queue keep running everything, and the nightly selection audit compares selected against full.
# ''The scrypt cost'': custody-law tests keep the real cost (never cut); every other fixture loads keys derived once per run and cached as test fixtures; no test knob in product code, no new environment variable.
# ''Mutation from advisory to gate'': by evidence, not a date: a package's mutation floor gates once it reads the same score across three consecutive nightly runs; until then it reports in the lane receipt; from then, every cut passes kill-set containment.
# ''The nightly budget'': at most twice one full develop run; incremental mutation over packages changed since the last nightly, a full re-run only when a floor moves or a package's tests change shape; a nightly past budget names what it skipped.
# ''The pilot'': the mutation pilot on `lares-cli` (lowest tooling risk; it answers whether Stryker carries this repo's TypeScript and vitest, `tools/law-mutants.mjs` the fallback), while node's run-wide kept houses (the largest sink) start beside it, proven by unchanged test and assertion counts and the law mutants still killed.

Found the same night and cured at once: 81 of develop's last 100 CI runs died cancelled because the called `e2e-shards.yml` cancelled on every push (PR #328).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/measure`>>

