````text
# Test estate, measured (2026-11-19)

Estate-Seer: Lares (Tasked Spirit). Read-only survey of `origin/develop` at `452cb7acb`. No suite ran; every
duration below comes off GitHub's own records or off the vitest JSON reports CI uploads.

## Sources and limits

| Source | What it gave |
|---|---|
| `git ls-files` at `452cb7acb` | file counts by package and kind |
| CI run `44497221032` (sha `a4dd6787`, all four test cells and all e2e shards green) | job and step seconds; artifacts `test-cell-*` and `e2e-shard-*` (vitest JSON, per-file and per-test durations); the `Witness cell rest` job log |
| CI runs `44508850912`, `44493309321` | job-seconds spread across three full runs |
| Held-out run `44508850648` | 24 held-out cells' seconds |
| `gh run list --branch develop --limit 100` (CI and Held-out) | conclusions and wall over a 15 h span, 2026-11-18T20:35Z to 2026-11-19T11:33Z |
| regex scans over tracked `*.test.ts` | setup-pattern, sleep, clock, port and timeout site counts |

Limits a reader should hold:

- **Prior research unread.** `lares tiddler get lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/research/test-estate-astra --meme` answered
  `control-home-unavailable: vessel-locked`; no copy stands on disk. The #/subsumption list never entered this survey, so
  the redundancy clusters below rest on names, titles and timings alone.
- **One run feeds the per-file numbers.** Per-file seconds come from run `44497221032` on idle 4-vCPU hosted runners.
  The desk (10 cores, load 6 to 25 tonight) runs slower by an unmeasured factor.
- **Vitest JSON hides hook time.** A file's reported span covers its test bodies; `beforeAll` stands and module import
  fall outside it. Where shard wall exceeds summed test seconds, the gap reads as hook and stand cost (inferred).
- **Pattern scans count regex sites**, never executed code paths. They undercount helpers that wrap a founding under
  another name.
- Redundancy clusters name candidates by shape. No cluster here stands verified as safely removable.

