### Run outcomes on develop

Over the last 100 CI runs (15 hours):

| Conclusion | Runs | Summed run wall | Median |
|---|---|---|---|
| cancelled | 81 | 522 min | 212 s |
| failure | 12 | 502 min | 2,255 s |
| success | 5 | 212 min | 2,261 s |

- Nine cancelled runs died after 10 minutes or more, two after 25 or more. Run `44499398019` stopped at 10:17:22Z after
  1,889 s, one second after the next push raised run `44504255940` at 10:17:21Z.
- `ci.yml` sets `cancel-in-progress` false for develop and says the run in flight must finish. The called
  `e2e-shards.yml` carries its own group `e2e-shards-${{ github.ref }}` with `cancel-in-progress: true`, keyed on the
  caller's ref. That group stands as the only cancel rule matching develop, so it reads as the probable cause
  (inferred from the two files and the timestamps; I never read a cancellation event's own attribution).
- Held-out over the same span: 84 cancelled, 14 success, 1 failure.
- `Witness cell rest` failed in all three completed full runs sampled. In run `44497221032` the log shows
  `evergreen-boundary-witness RED exit 1` (narration 1 over ceiling 0, version 1 over 0) and the self-tests at
  `pass 1327, fail 1`. A standing red in the witness gate caps the success count regardless of test wall time.

## Bottleneck shape: setup cost against assertion count

- **Cheap majority, costly tail.** 76% of tests finish under 50 ms. The 20 files at 60 s or more hold 2,682 s; the
  1,700 files under 1 s hold 169 s. Deleting or merging fast tests buys almost nothing in wall time.
- **Node pays per test, inside the test body.** Node averages 0.97 s per test against mesh at 0.05 s. 203 node tests
  exceed 5 s and 36 exceed 10 s. Files with `beforeEach` hold 1,454 of node's 3,813 s; files with `beforeAll` hold 249 s.
  Setup repeats per test far more often than it stands once per file.
- **Founding and stand helpers concentrate the cost.** 62 node files call a founding rite (`foundVessel`, `foundFace`,
  `foundCustody`, `foundDirect`; 253 sites) and hold 1,317 s. `withLarRoot` appears at 296 sites in 52 files.
  `keepHouse` reaches 18 node files (37 sites, 424 s), so the pattern that cut one suite 965 s to 531 s still has most
  founding files ahead of it.
- **E2E pays in hooks.** The `tests` set's four shards span 5,512 s of wall while their test bodies sum to 2,427 s.
  About 3,085 s (56%) falls outside test bodies, which matches 46 of 47 files carrying a `beforeAll` (the staged-vessel stand)
  with `fileParallelism: false`.
- **Web multiplies by engine.** 760 s of non-e2e web time comes from running the same files under two or three engines.
- **Mesh and tw5 stay cheap.** 1,002 files and 9,092 tests cost 675 s. `bootTestWiki` appears in 91 tw5 files (224
  sites) that together hold 103 s, so a TW5 boot per file costs little.

Projection, not measurement: summing CI's per-package walls gives about 68 min for a serial `pnpm test`, about 92 min
for the `tests` e2e set, and about 18 min for witnesses and self-tests on an idle 4-vCPU box.

