Only 52 test titles repeat across files (138 file-title pairs of 19,058), so literal duplication stays rare. The
redundancy that costs wall time sits in the same behavior re-proved at a costlier tier, never in copied tests.

## Flake classes

| Class | Measured | Named instances |
|---|---|---|
| A. 5 s default timeout under load | mesh, tw5, cli, memetic-frame, mempalace and sensorium configs set no `testTimeout`. On an idle runner, tests at 2.5 s or more: cli 100, tw5 20, mesh 12 | `filter-cts` 3.7 s (74% of budget idle), `surface-host` 2.8 s; neither file carries an explicit timeout |
| B. Statistical and cost assertions | `toBeLessThan` over seeded statistics and cost flatness | `coupling-nulls` (6 tests), `seal-cost-flat` (2 tests) |
| C. Fixed sleeps | 427 sites in 220 files; files holding them carry 4,326 test-s | `tests/e2e` 80 sites, node 107, tw5 55; `tools/*.sh` 28 `sleep N` |
| D. Wall clocks | 332 sites in 120 test files; evergreen witness reads `clock 52/52`, 23 excepted | `tests/e2e` 95 sites in 26 files |
| E. Ports and child processes | 173 listener sites in 69 files; 143 spawn sites in 76 files | node 121 listener sites; "already in use" named in `TEST-ARCHITECTURE.md` |
| F. Contention between suites | node `heavy` roster of 77 serial files; `pnpm test` runs `--workspace-concurrency=1` because packages share python holders | several spirits on one desk break the single-owner assumption the serialization encodes |
| G. Silent skip on stale dist | 303 skip-family sites in 219 files; 53 tests pending in the sampled run | `vitest-dist-guard` global setup; tw5 holds 181 of the sites |
| H. Hand-tuned timeouts | 1,528 explicit timeout sites in 513 files | node 489, tw5 422, `tests/e2e` 178 |
| I. CI plumbing | 81 of 100 runs cancelled; witness gate red in 3 of 3 sampled runs | `e2e-shards.yml` concurrency group; `evergreen-boundary-witness` |

Fake timers appear at 41 sites in 26 files, against 427 sleep sites.

## What coverage exists

- **No line, branch or mutation-score tooling.** No vitest `coverage` block, c8, istanbul, nyc or stryker anywhere in
  the workspace configs or workflows.
- **Law tests.** `packages/lares-cli/tests/laws/` holds 18 `*.law.test.ts` files with a fixed seed. 39 files across the
  estate carry "law" in their name (cli 19, mesh 7, tw5 7, keyhive 1, tools 5).
- **Hand-written mutants.** `tests/laws/mutants.json` names 14 mutants; `law-mutants-witness.sh` runs each against the
  laws that guard it (60 s in CI) through `vitest.law-mutants.config.ts`.
- **Partition laws on the runner itself.** The Test and E2E gates fail closed when a tracked file ran in no cell, ran
  twice, reported empty, or reported unparseable. This proves every file ran, never what the files cover.
- **Property tests.** `fast-check` appears in 7 files (12 sites). Snapshots appear at 5 sites.
- **Type coverage of tests.** `typecheck-tests-witness` (15 s) compiles every package's tests.
- **Ratio of tests to source.** 2,142 test files stand over 1,291 source `.ts` files in the seven main packages; mesh
  runs 597 test files over 437 sources, node 629 over 300.

A design that trades tests for wall time has no instrument today that reports what a removed test covered. The 14
mutants cover the CLI law tables alone.

